{"tool_name":"gbat","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gbat","home":"https://github.com/xuanyao/GBAT","summary":"A gene-based association test for robust detection of trans-gene regulation.\n\nThe observation that disease-associated genetic variants typically reside outside of exons has inspired widespread investigation into the genetic basis of transcriptional regulation.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T10:38:11Z","last_update_date":"2021-01-22T17:48:10Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gbat","credit":[{"email":"NZaitlen@mednet.ucla.edu","name":"Noah Zaitlen","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"xuanyao@uchicago.edu","name":"Xuanyao Liu","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Collapsing methods","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3791"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"}]}],"name":"GBAT","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-020-02120-1","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s).The observation that disease-associated genetic variants typically reside outside of exons has inspired widespread investigation into the genetic basis of transcriptional regulation. While associations between the mRNA abundance of a gene and its proximal SNPs (cis-eQTLs) are now readily identified, identification of high-quality distal associations (trans-eQTLs) has been limited by a heavy multiple testing burden and the proneness to false-positive signals. To address these issues, we develop GBAT, a powerful gene-based pipeline that allows robust detection of high-quality trans-gene regulation signal.","authors":[{"name":"Battle A."},{"name":"Dahl A."},{"name":"He Y."},{"name":"Liu X."},{"name":"Mefford J.A."},{"name":"Price A.L."},{"name":"Subramaniam M."},{"name":"Zaitlen N."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2020-08-24T00: